# The vendored C is stored byte for byte as upstream published it.
#
# `-text` turns off end-of-line normalisation for these trees. Without it git
# rewrites the CRLF files libsodium ships — its MSVC solutions, project files,
# `resource.rc` — to LF on the way in, and the working tree stops being
# byte-identical to the upstream commit `tools/build-tox.ps1` names.
#
# That matters here for one concrete reason: `patches/` is a diff against those
# commits, and a re-cut against a normalised tree would carry whitespace changes
# that have nothing to do with the fix. It also lets anyone check the trees
# against upstream with a plain `diff -r` and get only our two patches back.
/vendor/c-toxcore/** -text
/vendor/libsodium/** -text
